WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.440
<v Instructor>So here's a quick lecture</v>

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.840
around an architecture for DataSync.

3
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.510
So how do you access DataSync service

4
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.010
if you have a Direct Connect connection

5
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.590
and you wanna access it privately?

6
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.770
Well, to do it, we need to go through the VPC,

7
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.500
so the DataSync agent connects to Direct Connect

8
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.030
and here we have two options.

9
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.430
If we were to use a public VIF,

10
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.530
then we would go around the VPC

11
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.080
and use the public URL of the DataSync service,

12
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.580
so this may not be what we want.

13
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.160
Instead, what we have to do is to create

14
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.320
a VPC interface endpoint

15
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.480
and a private link, so that you can establish

16
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.550
a private VIF between Direct Connect

17
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.910
and the private link, so that the DataSync agent

18
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.480
can go through Direct Connect to your VPC,

19
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.890
to the interface VPC endpoint into the DataSync service.

20
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.150
Okay, so that's it.

21
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.100
I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

